US-01: Interpret Imperfect Natural Language Questions
5 SP

As a business user, I want the chatbot to understand abbreviations, shorthand, and misspelled questions so that I can retrieve account information without using exact terminology.

Acceptance criteria
- Recognizes common abbreviations, typos, and shorthand.
- Maps questions to applicable REQ-01 through REQ-10 capabilities.
- Does not guess missing account identifiers, relationships, or data values.
- Validates against business-provided sample questions.


US-02: Handle Ambiguous Questions with Targeted Follow-ups
5 SP

As a business user, I want the chatbot to ask a specific clarification question when my request is unclear so that it retrieves information for the correct account.

Acceptance criteria
- Detects missing account numbers, country codes, and unclear account scope.
- Asks one concise, relevant follow-up at a time.
- Uses the clarification to continue the original request.
- Identifies requests outside the documented delivery scope instead of inventing answers.


US-03: Maintain Account Context Across Conversations
5 SP

As a business user, I want the chatbot to remember the current account during a conversation so that I do not need to repeat the account number for every question.

Acceptance criteria
- Retains the current account and relevant conversation scope.
- Resolves subsequent questions against the selected account.
- Supports multi-turn queries without unnecessary clarification.
- Does not carry context incorrectly between unrelated conversations.


US-04: Handle Account Switching and Context Reconfirmation
3 SP

As a business user, I want the chatbot to recognize when I switch accounts so that subsequent responses use the correct customer information.

Acceptance criteria
- Identifies when a new account is introduced.
- Updates the active account context.
- Requests reconfirmation when multiple accounts could apply.
- Prevents data from the previous account being used incorrectly.


Feature 2 – Dynamic Output & Excel Export
US-05: Display Dynamic Results in Chatbot UI
5 SP

As a business user, I want account information displayed dynamically in the chatbot so that I can review the requested details clearly.

Acceptance criteria
- Displays applicable account fields in a readable format.
- Supports varying response fields and account types.
- Presents multiple account results clearly.
- Shows unavailable information without generating fabricated values.


US-06: Export Customer Account Results to Standardized Excel
8 SP

As a business user, I want to export the retrieved account information to Excel so that I can share and analyze results using the approved standard layout.

Acceptance criteria
- Provides an Excel export option for in-scope answers.
- Uses the approved golden Excel artifact with consistent tabs and columns for every account.
- Preserves accurate values and the applicable account identifiers.
- Supports unavailable fields in the standard format.
- Does not allow external emailing of exported data through the application.


US-07: Handle Unavailable and Out-of-Scope Fields
3 SP

As a business user, I want unavailable or out-of-scope information clearly identified so that I can distinguish missing data from valid account values.

Acceptance criteria
- Shows blank or N/A according to the approved field rules.
- Keeps the standard Excel schema even when fields are unavailable.
- Does not infer or manufacture missing data.
- Ensures consistent values between chatbot display and Excel export.


Feature 3 – Response Traceability & Explanation
This is especially relevant to your work with the watsonx Orchestrate agent and the Shippy React interface.
US-08: Capture Agent Execution Traceability and Data Sources
8 SP

As a business user, I want to understand which account, requirement, and data sources were used to generate a response so that I can verify its accuracy.

Acceptance criteria
- Captures the account used for each response.
- Records which requirement or intent was matched.
- Identifies the source used for each returned field, where source metadata is available.
- Records whether conversation context or account relationships were reused.
- Identifies unavailable fields and the reason when known.
- Does not present fabricated execution information.


US-09: Display Collapsible Response Explanation in Chatbot
5 SP

As a business user, I want to expand a traceability section beneath every answer so that I can review how the chatbot obtained the information.

Acceptance criteria
- Provides an automatically displayed collapsible explanation section with data answers.
- Shows the matched requirement, account, field sources, and relevant execution steps.
- Allows users to ask further questions about the explanation.
- Keeps the existing chatbot response format intact.


Implementation distinction: REQ-15 can be fulfilled using observable agent execution events, source provenance, and concise explanations. This is different from exposing the model's private internal chain-of-thought, which is not reliably available as an execution trace.
Feature 4 – Data Access Control
US-10: Enforce Authorization for Customer Data Retrieval
8 SP

As an authorized business user, I want the chatbot to enforce account data access permissions so that sensitive customer information is available only to approved users.

Acceptance criteria
- Validates user authorization before releasing account data.
- Enforces permissions in the backend, not only in the UI.
- Prevents unauthorized retrieval through alternate account queries.
- Applies the same access restrictions to Excel exports and traceability details.


US-11: Handle Unauthorized Data Access Requests
3 SP

As a business user, I want a clear response when I am not authorized to view account information so that protected data remains secure.

Acceptance criteria
- Returns no protected account data to unauthorized users.
- Displays a suitable access-denied message without leaking sensitive details.
- Supports positive and negative permission test cases.
- Implements field masking only if the business confirms that requirement.
